  "result": "I fixed two bugs, both in `total()` in `src/cart.js`, and all 243 tests now pass. I didn't touch any tests.\n\n1. **Wrong order:** tax was added first and the discount taken off afterwards. The comment in the code says the discount should come off the pre-tax subtotal. With percent discounts the order doesn't change the answer, which is why only the fixed-discount test failed (90 vs. the expected 88). Now the discount is applied first, then tax.\n2. **Negative totals:** a fixed discount bigger than the subtotal gave a negative total (-14.5). The discounted subtotal is now clamped at zero with `Math.max(0, …)`.\n\n`applyDiscount` on its own can still return a negative number. The zero floor is only enforced inside `total()`, which is the only place that uses it.",
